.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH gitaway-profile 1  "gitaway 0.0.0" "gitaway manual"
.SH NAME
gitaway\-profile \- Add, list, show, change and remove profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgitaway profile\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add, list, show, change and remove profiles
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
gitaway\-profile\-add(1)
Create a profile. Asks for anything not given as a flag
.TP
gitaway\-profile\-list(1)
List profiles. The default is marked with `*`
.TP
gitaway\-profile\-show(1)
Show a profile\*(Aqs settings
.TP
gitaway\-profile\-remove(1)
Delete a profile
.TP
gitaway\-profile\-default(1)
Make a profile the default, used when nothing more specific applies
.TP
gitaway\-profile\-set(1)
Change one setting, keeping the file\*(Aqs comments and layout
